  "identifier": "hover-net",
  "name": "HoVer-Net",
  "description": "Simultaneous nucleus instance segmentation and classification model for H&E histology images. Uses horizontal and vertical distance maps (HoVer maps) from nuclear centroids to separate touching nuclei, enabling accurate instance segmentation across dense tissue. Multi-branch architecture outputs segmentation mask, classification map, and HoVer maps in a single forward pass. Pretrained on CoNSeP (colon), PanNuke (pan-cancer, 19 tissue types), MoNuSAC, and Kumar/CPM datasets. MIT licensed, 712 stars, 272 forks. Published in Medical Image Analysis 2019. Developed at the Tissue Image Analytics (TIA) Centre, University of Warwick.",
  "url": "https://github.com/vqdang/hover_net",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/vqdang/hover_net",
  "relatedLink": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.media.2019.101563"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
